# clang-tidy 18, the tidy gate (ADR-0004). Disabled checks and why:
# - readability-magic-numbers: calendar code is full of numbers the spec names (1901, 12, 32); a
#   constant for each would hide them, not explain them.
# - readability-identifier-length: the spec's algorithms use single-letter names (y, m, d), and
#   loops use i; renaming them would drift from the text the code transcribes.
# - clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling: it asks for the Annex K
#   functions (snprintf_s, memcpy_s), which C11 makes optional and glibc, musl and Apple's libc
#   don't provide. The library calls none of these functions; the tools and tests pass a size to
#   every call.
# - bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters: the API takes (year, month, day) in the spec's order, and
#   the tools take (path, content) pairs; the check can't be met without wrapping each integer or
#   string in a struct.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  cert-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling,
  misc-*,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  readability-*,
  -readability-magic-numbers,
  -readability-identifier-length
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
HeaderFilterRegex: '(include|src|tools|tests)/'
